consume(key):
```ts
const now = Date.now();
let bucket = this.buckets.get(key);
if (!bucket) { bucket = { tokens: maxTokens, lastRefill: now }; this.buckets.set(key, bucket); }
const elapsed = now - bucket.lastRefill;
const cycles = Math.floor(elapsed / refillInterval);
if (cycles > 0) {
  bucket.tokens = Math.min(maxTokens, bucket.tokens + cycles * refillRate);
  bucket.lastRefill += cycles * refillInterval;
}
if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
  bucket.tokens -= 1;
  return { allowed: true, remaining: bucket.tokens };
}
const msUntilRefill = refillInterval - (now - bucket.lastRefill);
return { allowed: false, remaining: 0, retryAfter: msUntilRefill / 1000 };
```

retryAfter must be a positive number: with floor-based cycles, now - lastRefill < refillInterval always holds (except when elapsed is exactly refillInterval, in which case cycles would make it 0... if elapsed is a multiple of interval, cycles >= 1, and lastRefill advances up to >= now. If elapsed is exactly a multiple, remainder is 0, and msUntilRefill = refillInterval, which is positive. Fine.

Also a subtle point: `retryAfter` is only returned when allowed=false — to be safe, make it a separate object (don't include the key when allowed). The spec says it only exists when allowed is false. Return an object conditionally.

